## Repository grounding

At authoring, only PRD.md exists outside Git metadata. There is no implementation, package manifest, test suite, initial commit, or project instruction/ADR file. All source paths and exported symbols named by these tickets are **proposed contracts**. PRD line references are real; line numbers for nonexistent source are deliberately omitted.

Issue 1 establishes the pinned SDK mapping and conventions. Each downstream agent reads the prerequisite implementation and its tests rather than assuming a nonexistent example. A normal implementation may add necessary supporting files, but must preserve the approved slice boundaries and public behavior.

These files are the implementation backlog for building the plugin. The plugin's future generated feature issues live under `.ralph/features/<feature-id>/issues/`, as the PRD specifies; do not confuse the two locations.

